    "content": "All 18 checklist items have been tested and recorded (confirmed complete: 18/18).\n\n**Summary:** 10 PASS, 8 FAIL.\n\nCore viewing/browsing/visualization features work well (search/filter, model detail view, drag-reposition, template browsing, graph rendering, critical-path highlighting, coverage recalculation, risk-gap detection with a prominent alert, and UI responsiveness). However, the editing/persistence layer is largely broken: edge weights aren't editable at all, node enable/disable toggles give no visual feedback and behave inconsistently, applying a template only updates labels/stats without loading the actual graph, saving a custom template captures no name/description and isn't retrievable, explicit Save doesn't persist edits across navigation, running a scenario simulation shows no measurable impact on any indicator, and there's no way to create new edges (making the \"no edges to/from disabled nodes\" constraint untestable). These represent the highest-priority defects for remediation."
